                "fallback": "+327% more citations… Why translated websites win in AI search.  We just published our latest multilingual SEO\/GEO study, and found some surprising results on how AI Overviews treat translated sites.… | Eugene Ernoult",
                "text": "+327% more citations… Why translated websites win in AI search.\n\nWe just published our latest multilingual SEO\/GEO study, and found some surprising results on how AI Overviews treat translated sites.\n\nThe short version?\n\n𝗧𝗿𝗮𝗻𝘀𝗹𝗮𝘁𝗲𝗱 𝘄𝗲𝗯𝘀𝗶𝘁𝗲𝘀 𝗮𝗿𝗲 𝗰𝗿𝘂𝘀𝗵𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝗶𝘁.\n\nWe analyzed 1.3M+ citations across Google’s AI Overviews and found that translated pages are:\n\n:white_check_mark: 327% more visible for translated queries than non-translated pages\n:white_check_mark: Outperforming non-translated pages across the board\n\n𝗖𝗵𝗲𝗿𝗿𝘆 𝗼𝗻 𝘁𝗵𝗲 𝗰𝗮𝗸𝗲?\n\n:white_check_mark: Translated websites are cited more frequently across 𝘢𝘭𝘭 languages included in the study. We saw 𝟮𝟰% 𝗺𝗼𝗿𝗲 𝗰𝗶𝘁𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻𝘀 𝗽𝗲𝗿 𝗾𝘂𝗲𝗿𝘆 𝗼𝘃𝗲𝗿𝗮𝗹𝗹.\n\nHaving a translated website boosts your localized visibility and your visibility in your site's original language.\n\nFor marketers, this confirms what we’ve been seeing for months:\n\nMultilingual presence isn’t just about search rankings anymore, it’s key to standing out in AI-generated results too.\n\n:bar_chart: Want to dig into the data?\nLink to the full study in comments\n\nShoutout to Elizabeth for leading this key study, and our study partner, Ellipsis®! :blue_heart:",
